{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543728-is-koldunic-sorcery-op","id":1543728,"title":"Is Koldunic Sorcery OP?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-13T21:37:10-07:00","id":1543728,"title":"Is Koldunic Sorcery OP?","content":"In a lot of the games I have come across online everyone always seems to think/say that koldunic sorcery is really powerful. What is the consensus here? Do you think it\u2019s over powered? And how have you dealt with it at your table as either a player or storyteller?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","name":"Carsusbloodking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T00:00:55-07:00","id":1543738,"title":"","content":"Koldunic Sorcery is elemental magic based on spirits<br /> You don't learn Koldunic Sorcery by sitting in your dusty library studying scrolls and tomes like with Blood Magic, you have to go out and work and learn &quot;on the field&quot;<br /> Literally<br /> You slowly become acquainted with the spirits of the land, you learn what makes these entities tick, what they like and dislike, what piques their interest and how they can be called for aid or manipulated<br /> You make deals<br /> Unlike other sorceries that make use of Power of Will and formula or a blasphemy Shrine to a supposedly Godly Patron or systematic violation of taboos kaldunism makes use of environment and <i>Lore - </i>Tales and stories, floklore based superstitions passed from mother to child<br /> There are some rules variations here with some books insisting that Koldunism is a separate knowledge others treating it as an occult specialty and others treating it as a regular discipline requiring an attribute plus an occult roll<br /> But the theme reamins - it is a knowledge you have to work for<br /> Depending on the type of spirit being called to aid the practice itself is based on lore on the practitioner's familiarity and connection with spirits and ability to manipulate them<br /> Koldunism is the closest in Vampire how the Garou operate<br /> To learn their Gifts and Rites a Garou basically have to do the same what a Koldun have to do to learn - became familiar with the Spirits, explore the Land, respect and honor the land, the traditions, the history and make bargains and deals, <i>earn </i>the trust and fear of the Spirits and pay their price<br /> <br /> Overpowered? Maybe<br /> In the right hand<br /> But to be a Koldun, you have to know the proper &quot;protocol&quot; when you deal with Spirits.<br /> The Storyteller and players can get really creative with that protocol since it isn't described in detail in any of the books.<br /> It can consist of gestures or sigils or sounds verbal commands in dead languages maybe instruments that resonate with the spirit being called forth but the procedure will always differ from element to element<br /> One does not call out to living flame in the same way they call out to the spirits of the wind!<br /> Understanding the proper way and the safe way to interact with the Spirits and enlist their aid without rousing their wrath can take decades and depends a lot on the region<br /> The spirits themselves - though they might be of the same element the Koldun is already familiar with - differ from land to land<br /> The water spirits of the Black Sea are not the same as the water spirits of the Mediterranean Sea or those of a river like the Volga<br /> <br /> Among the Tzimisce who are tied to their Land the Koldun have the deepest connection and on a strange, unfamilar land far from their home they have tremendous difficulities to use their magic - sometimes it is impossible to properly use their ways - untill they became familiar with the local spirits and bargained and made deals to get on their good side<br /> <br /> So Koldunism could be considered overpowered yes<br /> But it is well balanced by how you should use it, learn it and basically build your unlife around it<br /> It is not like Thaumaturgy or Necromancy (tho' necromancy is the closest since you have to do the rituals and the legwork, gather information about the Wraiths and Specters like how a Koldun works with Spirits and sometimes Banes but the difference is the approach: a Koldun and the Spitits are working together, a Necromancer and her ghost are a slave and master relationship based on hatred and threats) where you pack up your books and just move... when a Koldun is forced to abbandon her domain that is going back to square one basically and start everything from scratch. <br /> <br /> (Not to mention if your ST is in to it a Koldun should attract the attention to the local Garou/Lupine community (and more often than not a Koldun could do a better job than the Claws of Gaia witch could lead to very funny situations where the Spirits themselves smack the nose of the wolfs to &quot;hands off of my Partner&quot; and could lead to rivalries or strange bedfellow teamups against serious dark spirits) )\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-14-2024, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T07:43:45-07:00","id":1543749,"title":"","content":"There is also the fact that Koldunic Sorcery was created later in the games development cycle, which means the mechanics are more streamlined than Thaumaturgy and its functions feel more cinematic. A good example of this is comparing The Lure of Flames Thaumaturgy path to the Koldunic Way of Fire, the mechanics are far more useful and varied in the Koldunic setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T08:58:28-07:00","id":1543757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543728-is-koldunic-sorcery-op?p=1543749#post1543749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the fact that Koldunic Sorcery was created later in the games development cycle, which means the mechanics are more streamlined than Thaumaturgy and its functions feel more cinematic. A good example of this is comparing The Lure of Flames Thaumaturgy path to the Koldunic Way of Fire, the mechanics are far more useful and varied in the Koldunic setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside the lore implications regarding its use, that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> writen and put it very well, this is the main &quot;problem&quot; I see in my experience as a ST, koldunic sorcery was developped latter and made much superior to anything standard Thaumaturgy can do and for more than 2 decades I've heard players complaining about how disappointed they are that so many Thaumaturgy Paths are so bland like Creo Ignem and Rego Motus, but then you have Koldunic Sorcery do it ten times better and, perhaps more importantly, more interesting and flashy. Not to mention with Kodunic Sorcery you basically have a nuke stated with rules in the form of &quot;Jaws of the Dracon&quot;, hell even an acomplished master mage would have a lot of trouble replicating that and no other school of blood sorcery got anything remotely close to that. Basically, as one friend of mine once told me, it feels almost as if the developpers were trolling the Tremere (and to a lesser extent, other blood magicians) on purpose. But don't get me wrong, I love the powers and all the lore surrounding them, I just feel that a good buff to Thaumaturgy Paths should have been made if the developers wanted anything resembling a distant faint of &quot;balance&quot; in the setting, but since I've been houseruling almost everything in the game for more than 10 years, that's not a big deal to me and my groups, I just adapt the ideas and present them to my players my way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 10-14-2024, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T11:40:35-07:00","id":1543772,"title":"","content":"It also really depends on which form of &quot;Koldunic Sorcery&quot; you mean. There are the Old ways with Kraina and what are essentially spirits gifts/rites instead of rituals, and then there are the New ways which are much closer to thaumaturgy with a more elemental focus.<br /> <br /> New Koldunism, I have to say no for the same reason I think thaumaturgy is under-powered despite the bad rep, it's a massive XP sink to do anything useful and is often weaker than equivalent XP spent in disciplines.<br /> <br /> Old Koldunism is actually a solid &quot;Maybe&quot;, but it's not a given thing. Old rites can be really strong and cost Blood+WP to learn rather than XP, but they also come with their own internal balancing in the form of bans. Either way I like this style better, having to gain weaknesses to gain more powers is actually a really cool idea for vampire powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T11:50:21-07:00","id":1543774,"title":"","content":"Meh. Thaumaturges have dozens and dozens of paths and rituals, and Thaumaturgy is in-clan for Tremere (rituals are free). Kolduns are much more limited in what they can learn, and Koldunism is out-of-clan.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Koldunism requires a variety of attributes to use, while Thaumaturgy Paths only use Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T14:06:07-07:00","id":1543779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> New Koldunism, I have to say no for the same reason I think thaumaturgy is under-powered despite the bad rep, it's a massive XP sink to do anything useful and is often weaker than equivalent XP spent in disciplines. </div> </div> </div>I agree with that completely, because it's almost always going to be inferior to Disciplines. Especially considering most people use celerity as raw (something that astonish me as multiple actions UTTERLY break the ST system and that's why I banned it long time ago and I consider that one of the best things both in Requiem and in V5), because I'm saying disregarding celerity + potence utter broken combo, that is EVEN WHEN WE DON'T ALLOW multiple actions through celerity and stuff, both Thaumaturgy and Koldunism pale in comparisson to them, now if you consider them there's not even the slightest chance of reasonably comparing such things. What I was saying is that compared to standard Thaumaturgy Koldunic Sorcery makes it look like a silly thing and makes one wonder what the main argument for Tremere success was during the first editions, i.e. presenting a unified blood magic front with innovative powers, etc. was all about. Why bother playing a Tremere locked under the oprressive structure of the clan when you can be a badass fire sorcerer who can from the get go deal fire damage compared to mage against other vampires who are particularly vulnerable to fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T14:45:39-07:00","id":1543783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, Koldunism requires a variety of attributes to use, while Thaumaturgy Paths only use Willpower. </div> </div> </div>This is in fact more a limiting factor than anything (and I suspect it's the main reason they made Jaws of the Dracon roll Willpower + Occultism, as otherrwise ancient beings would be limited to a mere 10 dice pool). Rolling willpower can be certainly better when we talk about 13 generation vampires, but not really in a dark ages chronicle where you can start on 7th generation and quite easily surpass the limiting 10 dice pool...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T16:00:46-07:00","id":1543788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543728-is-koldunic-sorcery-op?p=1543738#post1543738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You slowly become acquainted with the spirits of the land, you learn what makes these entities tick, what they like and dislike, what piques their interest and how they can be called for aid or manipulated</div> </div> </div> </div>Like all powers that require a much more active ST to adjudicate things on the fly, it can be very easy for the ST to not portray it right and just give too much discretion to the PC so that other players start complaining about that character being overpowered.<br /> <br /> Even in Werewolf, the spirit world can put a lot of extra burden onto the ST. The ST needs to create another world of spirits out there, figure out spirit broods, character reputations, determine what they want and so on. I've seen a lot of Werewolf games where the ST just handwaves this - despite it supposedly being a critical element of the Werewolf setting - because it's too much work, they don't feel adequately prepared to roleplay it, and players may not demand it or worse, heavily disagree with the ST's approach. So a lot of the supposed complexity and balance of the game just gets thrown out.<br /> <br /> So to put such a thing in vampire, where that aspect of the setting doesn't come into play and many STs have no experience in running, seems like it is asking for trouble.<br /> <br /> It's very easy to say in an online forum, &quot;oh, this is balanced by the ST making additional roleplaying requirements&quot; than actually running the game that way.<br /> <br /> I've seen the same thing apply to Necromancy and ghosts in the underworld. STs often just default to &quot;yes, you can do that&quot; because they are already busy just with trying to master the Vampire setting, and don't have the same time or interest to put in the effort to understanding the underworld (whether it's the official Wraith version or a homebrew one). Or if other players complain too much, then all of a sudden the PC can't seem to do anything with the power. I think Astral Projection is also similar with the Astral Plane being handwaved because the setting doesn't provide much guidance to the ST.<br /> <br /> When I first played Vampire games, I had zero interest in learning about the other games or involving their elements into my Vampire chronicles. There was already so much lore about Vampire itself that I could barely keep track of that. It took a long time before I got to the point where I wanted to begin including select elements in my vampire games like having a haunted house, willing to deal with spirits for various blood magic, perhaps a dangerous area of town patrolled by Lupines, etc. My first attempts were not very successful in getting the right balance of doing it right and having the game be fun. I had to put in a lot more thinking of how to handle things.<br /> <br /> I do agree with your statements, but I also wanted to point out that this is not as easy in practice as it may sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T22:56:10-07:00","id":1543836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543728-is-koldunic-sorcery-op?p=1543788#post1543788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do agree with your statements, but I also wanted to point out that this is not as easy in practice as it may sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completly agree<br /> A Koldun is like the Huangan of the Voudoun Necromancy and the Lector Priests of the Akhu<br /> They are part of the local culture and community (more often than not to this day!)<br /> I am fortunate becasue my great great grandmother was a &quot;Koldun&quot; - or at least the local equivalent of it, a Solomonari; (could control some Elemental Spirits, they could curse and heal, they could conjure or banish clouds, they could call down hail storms even lightning using their Enchanted axes, spoke with the dead and the spirtis and kept evil at bay. They learned their magic from a mentor and some legends say they even had a school located beyond the shroud) - on our parts they were called &quot;Zeim (variant of Zmei) nitish &quot;Dragon Rider&quot; - and I love the fact it is VERY similar sound of the word Tzimisce<br /> A Koldun is not ideal for every play, like how a Huangan or a Lector Priest are not for every Game,<br /> You and your ST have to do your home work and it is tremendous extra work, not just like - and I don't want to offend anyone - a common Thaumaturgist or Necromancer (tho' as you pointed out Necromancy is the best if you know Wraith)<br /> But if you know the cultural background, what it <i>means</i> to be a Koldun, a Huangan or a Lector Priest?<br /> It is enrich the game tremendously and gives it an unimaginable depth\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T23:10:11-07:00","id":1543840,"title":"","content":"Clanbook Tzimisce Revised has my favorite Koldunic Sorcery power. The Way of Sorrow, specifically the third level the Weeping of Kruchina. You make your roll, spend a WP, GLARE at someone, and they start crying hysterically. Cainites lose a blood point per turn per success as they cry out vitae. A BP is about 500 ml give or take, and a turn is between 3 second and 3 minutes, so please imagine the copious amount of vitae just streaming out the poor victim's face.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"187\" height=\"140\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://giffiles.alphacoders.com/136/136600.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://giffiles.alphacoders.com/136/136600.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://giffiles.alphacoders.com/136/136600.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T23:43:11-07:00","id":1543844,"title":"","content":"Weeping of Kruchina is way more than weeping blood<br /> Karna was known by several names across the Slavic world, a reflection of her widespread worship. In Russian mythology, she was Karna, but she was also called Carna, Kruchina, and Kurnitsa in other Slavic regions.<br /> These names emphasized her role as the <b>personification of grief and sorrow</b>.<br /> When a Koldun invoke Her name and call her aid (or an apropiate Spirit of Sorrow) it makes more than force their victim to weep blood<br /> That is trivial compared to the <i><u>why</u></i><br /> Even the power actually spells this out, a depressing notion overcomes the victim, they might mourn their lost humanitas or the passing of lovers who died long ago or anything else<br /> The psychological effects and damage the really harsh, not the few rounds of weeping of torrents of blood<br /> It hurts the mind and the soul - because like with the Presence or Blood Blood, when if the effect wears out the <i>memory </i>of the feeling remains and gnaws on the soul and mind<br /> It is more brutal torment than twisting their flesh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 10-15-2024, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T23:47:47-07:00","id":1543845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do agree with your statements, but I also wanted to point out that this is not as easy in practice as it may sound. </div> </div> </div>Not only that, but people here are basically completely circumcenting the main point of the thread that is strictly systematic in nature. I'll try to be as concise as possible.<br /> <br /> Hermeticism, what Thaumaturgy, especially Tremere one is based upon has a really long tradition in real life and in the game publication history. It probably has at the very least 10 times more space dedicated to all its paradigms than Koldunism has in its whole history in the setting and it also encompass dealing with the spiritual world, with paths like Spiritual Manipulation, among others, totally dedicated to it, not to mention rituals, etc. I'm not even going to mention the fact that also in real life with would have much more publications on it than on &quot;koldunic sorcery&quot; (a weird name btw, but that's for another topic) and as such it has a really good potential (and always should whenever possible) to enrich the game tremendously.<br /> <br /> Again what is being discussed here is if it's &quot;op or not&quot;. As I stated, yes, from a systematic point of view, Koldunic Sorcery is not only more interesting than at least any of the &quot;most basic paths&quot;, like &quot;Creo Ignem&quot; and it's much more powerful to boost. So, it's certainly very easy to understand why so many people got and some still get bothered with the way it works in the game. It's not balance in the least. There's no way to compare &quot;Creo Ignem&quot; to &quot;Way of Fire&quot;. I onc saw a player deal 12 aggravated fire damage to another vampire with an initial character, using just level 2 of Way of Fire. While with &quot;Creo Ignem&quot; even at lv 5 you can at most deal 3/turn, it's laughably impossible to compare such a thing and that's probably why we see so many people complaining about it being &quot;op&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 10-15-2024, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"H