 to try to contain that demon.<br /> <br /> Kolduns, well, better be able to DEAL with that spirit, barter or beatings, to keep that spirit subservient. Spirits likely don't like being errand boys for some lazy vampire.<br /> <br /> Look into the various mythologies. Many shamans and such needed to strike deals or, die, to commune with spirits. That communion can get grisly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wouldn't that make Kolduns more like D&amp;D Warlocks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T17:44:40-07:00","id":1543935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tremere Thaumaturgy is like D&amp;D Wizards.<br /> <br /> Kolduns are like D&amp;D Sorcerer's. </div> </div> </div>Minus the part where both are actually balanced in some ways and in D&amp;D Wizard is by far the most powerful class at max lv, while in vampire what you call &quot;sorcerers&quot; are like 3 times better at every level and things get worse (for the Tremere) the lower the generation is lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:12:04-07:00","id":1544099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container